WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.629
– Michael Audrey Myers was born in 1957, as
the second, and FINAL child of Edith and Donald

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:07.915
Myers after his nine year old sister, Judith.

00:00:07.915 --> 00:00:11.299
In this video, I’m analyzing the latest
version of the Michael Myers character, from

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:12.380
the 40 Year Timeline.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.109
That includes Halloween, Halloween (2018),
Halloween Kills and Halloween Ends.

00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:20.689
Most cities have a union station or joint
station where most of their routes connect.

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:24.400
In the case of the Halloween Express, that
is Halloween (1978).

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.949
From there, you can go down the original route,
where Michael is involved with a cult worshiping

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.780
an ancient demon, you can go down the 20 Year
Timeline route, where Michael escapes after

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:35.540
getting blown up by Dr. Loomis, or you can
go down the 40 Year Timeline route, where

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.700
Michael is captured, and locked up for 4 decades.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.040
So his origin in this timeline is mostly a
familiar one… but not entirely.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.250
Things would take a twist.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.000
In this video, you’ll learn how this iteration
of Michael Myers was modeled after Jaws, the

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.130
meaning of his signature traits like the head
tilt and the answer to the one question on

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:55.260
everyone’s mind: is this the end of Michael
Myers?

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.990
To find out, stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:03.209
(metal music)

00:01:03.209 --> 00:01:05.810
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.670
One of the goals set by co-writers David Gordon-Green
and Danny McBride was to make the Michael

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.290
Myers character scary again.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:15.800
To do this, they looked back to the original,
which included no familial relations, no complex

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.680
backstories, and no ove explanations of the
character.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.200
Producer Jason Blum and David Gordon-Green
have both described their approach as walking

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.780
the line between honoring the old and twisting
that into something new.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.980
For example, Michael’s look and body language
are closer to that of the original than ever

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.100
before, but they weren’t opposed to ramping
up the blood and gore to keep up with the

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.560
modern slasher, something we didn’t really
see during Michael’s first appearance in

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.280
the more conservative 1970s.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.560
The most important direction for a contemporary
boogeyman was to re-introduce the mystique,

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.418
and that comes across in the way he’s written,
acted, and even in the design of his iconic mask.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.549
– [McBride] There’s something scary about
someone committing those kinds of violent

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:54.600
acts with no emotion at all, and that’s
what that mask does.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.350
You can project your own things that frighten
you onto that mask.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.370
Special FX designer Chris Nelson created the
mask with the goal of preserving the melancholy

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:06.210
of the character, and many fans agree that
it was effective in using a blank slate to

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.539
bring back the horror of what might be.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:13.540
Other timelines mess up the illusion of emotionlessness
by showing his face, making him cry, explaining

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:18.170
his childhood in great detail, or in some
cases, just using masks that look too surprised

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.170
or too angry.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.200
“I'd like to know as little about him or
his history and abilities as possible,”

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.810
the director offered (in an interview with
HalloweenMovies.com.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.290
“I think there was a reason he was called
The Shape in the original because in some

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.069
ways he's more of an essence than he is a
traditional character.”

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.010
While this is a valid point, I also think
that the very practice of doing a sequel trilogy

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.440
results in new lore being added to the character.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.506
This one goes back to the idea that Michael
Myers is human, but with a supernatural edge;

00:02:41.506 --> 00:02:42.849
he’s nearly invincible.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:48.010
– [Carpenter] A character who is between
human being and the supernatural.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.750
– And he’s a human being, we need to understand.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.530
– And with more scenes to study, we can start
to recognize patterns and draw a few conclusions

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:59.380
about him, without disrupting the mysterious
allure that has made him a legend for so many decades.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.218
We’ve got a lot of ground to cover, so let’s
get into it.

00:03:02.218 --> 00:03:06.000
(ominous piano)

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.410
As a child, Michael was an outcast.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:13.645
While he didn’t exhibit any alarming behavior,
he didn’t seem to exhibit much behavior at all. 

00:03:13.645 --> 00:03:17.330
This caused some adults to feel bad for him,
including the mother of a boy in his class,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.330
Peter McCabe.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.440
Mrs. McCabe would make her son go over to
Michael’s house to play, but Michael would

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.610
spend all of his time just staring out his
sister’s window.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.010
At the age of six years old, on October 31st,
1963.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.610
Michael’s parents go out for the evening,
and his older sister is hanging out with her

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.068
boyfriend, leaving him unsupervised.

00:03:32.068 --> 00:03:36.080
After seeing Judith and her boyfriend go upstairs,
he takes a knife from the kitchen and heads

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.080
up himself.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.040
Judith is combing her hair when the boy creeps
up and stabs her several times.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.340
He simply walks outside and stands in front
of the house as his parents come home to discover

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.340
his crime.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.980
He was taken into the custody of the Illinois
Department of Public Safety - Juvenile Justice

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:50.980
on November 1st.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:54.790
Officials at the time stated he likely would
not be charged with first-degree murder, pending

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.660
a psychological evaluation.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:00.180
After the evaluation, it was decided he would
undergo psychiatric treatment.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.300
Michael is labeled as patient number A-2201,
sentenced to Smith’s Grove Sanitarium and

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.780
assigned to a psychiatrist named Dr. Samuel
Loomis.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.600
His initial stay at Smith’s Grove lasted
15 years, none of which is documented in the

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.660
Halloween films.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.952
– Michael Audrey Myers shall be
brought before the court on the day of his

00:04:15.952 --> 00:04:20.120
21st birthday, where he shall be tried as
an adult.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.559
– For those who are wondering, this scene is
one of the extra scenes shot for the television

00:04:23.559 --> 00:04:25.950
version of the original 1978 film.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:30.069
Long story short, they wanted to add scenes
to fit a television time slot with more commercials.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:33.689
The question is, if these scenes are still
canon in the 40 Year Timeline, because in

00:04:33.689 --> 00:04:37.129
Halloween 2018, we see this: Michael’s middle
initial is A.

00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:40.099
The name Michael Audrey Myers comes from these
made for TV scenes.

00:04:40.099 --> 00:04:43.220
It’s totally possible that this was 
intended to be an easter egg though, because

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.770
another made for TV scene shows that Michael
wrote the word “sister” on his door before

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.199
breaking out of Smith’s Grove.

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:52.534
This suggests that he broke out to go after
his sister, Laurie, which he does in Halloween II.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:55.758
However, Michael and Laurie are not siblings
in the 40 Year Timeline.

00:04:55.758 --> 00:04:58.020
Co-writer Danny McBride has talked about this
change.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.729
“I was pushing for the removal of the familial
mythology set-up in Halloween 2 right off

00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:02.729
the bat.

00:05:02.729 --> 00:05:05.330
I just felt like it was an area where he wasn't
quite as scary anymore.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.740
It seemed too personalized.”

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.379
The idea was that the audience knows they’re
not related to Michael, so they didn't have anything

00:05:10.379 --> 00:05:11.379
to worry about.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:14.960
But if he’s just going after random people,
everyone has a reason to be afraid.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.099
It’s possible that Michael wrote “sister”
in reference to Judith, whose tombstone he

00:05:18.099 --> 00:05:19.280
steals after breaking out.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.360
So you could make an argument either way as
to the canonicity of these added scenes.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.009
My take is that they are not part of the 40
Year Timeline.

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:29.979
The extra scenes were shot using the crew
from Halloween II, and they aired in 1980,

00:05:29.979 --> 00:05:33.315
right before Halloween II, so it’s pretty
clear that they’re meant to set up that movie. 

00:05:33.315 --> 00:05:37.419
Halloween (2018) takes a strong stance in
that it only acknowledges Halloween 1, going

00:05:37.419 --> 00:05:39.969
so far as to say that Halloween II was just
made up.

00:05:40.684 --> 00:05:44.998
– [Dave] Wasn’t it her brother who, like,
cold blooded murdelated all those teenagers?

00:05:44.998 --> 00:05:46.291
– [Allyson] No.

00:05:46.291 --> 00:05:49.210
That’s just a bit that some people made
up to make them feel better I think.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:54.059
– In 1978, after Michael turned 21, he was due
back in court for re-evaluation, but when

00:05:54.059 --> 00:05:57.849
Dr. Loomis and his associate Nurse Marion
Chambers arrived to pick him up, he and several

00:05:57.849 --> 00:05:59.689
other patients were on the loose.

00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:02.469
Michael stole their car and escaped into the
night in Warren County.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:06.339
This version of the Michael Myers character
plays into his status as an urban legend.

00:06:06.339 --> 00:06:10.990
And it makes sense, because Halloween (2018),
Kills and Ends are aimed at a new generation.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:15.369
A generation who has probably heard of Michael
Myers, but not yet experienced him for themselves,

00:06:15.369 --> 00:06:16.749
much like an urban legend.

00:06:16.749 --> 00:06:18.819
Think about the popular urban legends of our
culture.

00:06:18.819 --> 00:06:20.999
There are always repeating elements and symptoms.

00:06:20.999 --> 00:06:25.120
Bloody Mary will appear if you say her name
into a mirror three times with only a candle’s light.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.399
Slenderman will appear nestled in forest trees
and cause glitches in video equipment.

00:06:29.399 --> 00:06:33.629
The lights will flicker on and off before
the appearance of The Hash Slinging Slasher.

00:06:33.629 --> 00:06:37.409
In Michael’s case, he comes out around Halloween
night, surrounded by a fleet of wraith-like

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:38.409
mental patients.

00:06:38.409 --> 00:06:41.719
There are many other symptoms of the urban
legend that are seen by multiple generations

00:06:41.719 --> 00:06:44.719
of Haddonfield residents, which I’ll point
out throughout this lesson.

00:06:44.719 --> 00:06:49.069
First example: in 1963, Michael had a one
piece clown suit, a mask and a knife; and

00:06:49.069 --> 00:06:51.990
he targeted a teenager who had been getting
busy with her boyfriend.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.159
So in 1978, the legend would continue with
Michael obtaining a one piece jumpsuit, a

00:06:56.159 --> 00:06:59.719
mask and a knife; and he would once again
target teenagers who are trying to do the

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.069
act, as stand-ins for Judith.

00:07:01.069 --> 00:07:04.152
He runs a mechanic’s truck off the road
and offs him to get the suit.

00:07:04.152 --> 00:07:08.129
To make this night a tribute to his last rampage,
he steals Judith’s tombstone from the cemetery.

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:11.689
He breaks into the general store to steal
a Halloween mask, and also gets some rope,

00:07:11.689 --> 00:07:12.744
which he would use later,

00:07:12.744 --> 00:07:15.963
in addition to picking up his now signature weapon, a couple of knives.

00:07:15.963 --> 00:07:18.610
His next stop is his childhood home, which
now sits abandoned.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:21.719
It is here that he gets hungry, and eats part
of a dog.

00:07:21.719 --> 00:07:25.490
And it is also here where he first encounters
Laurie Strode, a high school student who is

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:29.289
there to drop off a set of keys for her father,
who is a realtor trying to sell the property.

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:33.210
He follows her around all day until she arrives
at her babysitting job that evening.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:36.770
Her friend Annie is babysitting across the
street, and she becomes the next victim.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.899
Michael hides in her car, so when she goes
to pick up her boyfriend, he strangles her

00:07:39.899 --> 00:07:41.360
before she gets out of the garage.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.800
His next victims are Bob and Lynda, who are
trying to use the house as a private place

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.869
to do their thing.

00:07:45.869 --> 00:07:49.889
He arranges all three dead teens in the upstairs
bedroom with Annie on the bed under the Judith

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:53.569
Myers tombstone, making it clear that he’s
trying to recreate the scenario from his youth.

00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:56.462
He stuffs Lynda in a cupboard and hangs Bob
overhead in the closet.

00:07:56.462 --> 00:07:59.269
Then he kills the lights in the house and
waits for Laurie to notice

00:07:59.269 --> 00:08:01.050
and come over to check on her friends. 

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:05.453
When she does she’s demonstrably distrubed,
but her next find is even more horrifying.

00:08:11.497 --> 00:08:17.289
(screams)

00:08:17.289 --> 00:08:20.860
Michael slowly but methodically chases her
back across the street to the Doyle household

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:24.280
and makes several more attempts on her, but
she puts up a good fight, first stabbing him

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.759
in the neck with a knitting needle, then poking
his eye out with a clothing hanger and finally

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:29.789
stabbing him in the chest with the knife he
dropped.

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:34.650
But Michael Myers is far from any ordinary
man, and rises back to life in an almost vampire

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.650
like fashion.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.430
He gets ahold of his exhausted prey, finally
seeing his chance to end it by strangling

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:42.870
her, but she does something unexpected by
removing his mask.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.690
This causes him to stop momentarily and he
attempts to put it back on before continuing

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:47.495
to attack her.

00:08:47.495 --> 00:08:51.400
His fixation with the mask is never detailedly
explained, but it’s obviously an important

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:52.710
part of the process for him.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:56.640
In the original timeline, I analyzed the mask
as an important part of the ritualistic practice

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.960
he’s taking part in, but here in the 40
Year Timeline, Michael is simply an escaped

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:00.733
mental patient.

00:09:00.733 --> 00:09:04.640
It’s a common occurrence for mental patients
to respond poorly to any change outside their

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.640
comfortable normal.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:10.080
That’s why mental institutions never deviate
from having simple white walls with no decorations.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.985
The staff are always dressed identically,
with the same inoffensive music played every day.

00:09:13.985 --> 00:09:17.990
The same old boring facility actually creates
a calm, safe environment for the patients.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.090
We also see this with a character in the 40
Year Timeline, Mr. Tivoli.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:24.800
He has a fixation with tied shoelaces, and
anything else is upsetting to him.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.820
Michael was wearing a mask and one piece costume
when he killed his sister in 1963, so he feels

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:33.810
the need to wear similar attire, mask included,
to kill during the anniversary here in 1978,

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.460
and the same would be true in the future.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.636
But this little distraction ends up being
a much larger detour.

00:09:38.636 --> 00:09:39.584
– I shot him!

00:09:39.584 --> 00:09:41.129
I shot him six times!
I shot him!

00:09:41.129 --> 00:09:42.772
I shot him in the heart!
I shot him six times!

00:09:42.772 --> 00:09:44.360
Fired six shots into him.

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.960
– To this point, this would be the most damage
that Haddonfield’s boogeyman had ever taken

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.860
on, and it came at the hands of his own psychiatric
doctor, but it doesn’t keep him down for

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.435
long; he only needs a couple of seconds to
flee the scene and cut through an alley to escape.

00:09:55.435 --> 00:09:59.380
He is spotted by a timid young Officer Frank
Hawkins, who shoots at him, but an unphased

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.470
Michael simply walks away, out of sight.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:05.190
It seems the first thing he does after this
is move his car, because we can see it right

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.200
here, parked outside the old Myers house.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.900
Combine that with the breathing we hear at
the end of Halloween while looking across

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.120
the street at the house, and it seems likely
that this was the first place he went.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.071
If you think about it, it makes sense that
he’d try to repark the car, because he was

00:10:16.071 --> 00:10:20.010
just attacked by Dr. Loomis, who is the most
likely person to recognize that car.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:23.360
Michael goes back out on foot and comes across
a boy named Lonnie Elam, who had tripped on

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.360
the sidewalk.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.080
Michael doesn't kill kids, and he sees a pair
of police officers approaching, so once again,

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:31.830
he miraculously disappears, something he’s
managed to do a number of times now.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.400
He retreats into his old home and stands at
the window, just as he did as a child.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:39.320
The officers are McCabe, who Michael had play-dates
with in their youth, and Frank Hawkins, who

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.120
he had encountered not long before.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:45.032
They investigate the house where Michael surprises
McCabe, one of the few times we ever see him run.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.530
He slams the officer into the wall several
times and uses the remainder of the rope taken

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.150
from the hardware store to strangle him.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.650
We see McCabe manage to get in several good
punches in the abdomen, but Michael hardly

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:57.670
seems to notice, and takes him hostage just
before Hawkins gets into the room and shoots.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:01.820
But the rookie officer accidentally hits his
partner, rather than the masked perpetrator.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:05.060
Michael drops his meat shield, and calmly
walks out of the house, even as several more

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.530
shots are fired at him.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:11.080
This entire night, he’s been trying to recreate
the circumstances of his first kill in 1963,

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:14.601
and he brings it all to a close by walking
out of the house and standing in the front

00:11:14.601 --> 00:11:16.450
yard, just as he did back then.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.870
This time, he is immediately surrounded by
six armed police officers, who are able to

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:23.600
beat him down, capture him and return him
to captivity, this time in prison.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:27.150
“Shortly after Myers began his term in the
state prison, he was transferred from medium

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:30.460
to maximum security because he apparently
formulated escape plans.”

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:35.050
He also forged his own identification credentials,
took notes on airplane schedules and somehow

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.410
acquired road maps and a driver’s license.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.300
After shooting him six times, Loomis was removed
from his position as Michael Myers’s doctor.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.200
Whether this was voluntary or involuntary
is not known.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:49.900
In a statement recorded in audio on January
22nd 1979, about three months after the babysitter

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.738
murders, he suggests that Myers should get
the death penalty.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.070
– My suggestion is termination.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:12:00.090
Death is the only solution for Michael.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:03.410
– However, the state wanted to keep Michael
alive to be studied, hoping they could gain

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.190
more insight on the mind of a killer.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.850
This is probably why he was eventually returned
to Smith’s Grove.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:11.360
I like to think I’m doing a much better
job of that in this video than they did in

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.000
their 55 years of study.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.240
But as I mentioned, Michael is more of an
essence than an actual character.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:20.220
We can assume Loomis knew this, and kept watch
over Michael with only the intention of keeping

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:21.330
him locked up.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:25.250
However, he eventually passed away, and his
successor would not have the same intentions.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:29.430
The next psychiatrist assigned to look over
Michael is a man by the name of Dr. Ranbir Sartain.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:33.570
Dr. Sartain became obsessed with trying to
understand Michael and his motives and abilities.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:37.220
This causes Sartain to develop a bond to his
patient and become protective of him, the

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.550
same way an artist might defend their own
life’s work.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:43.560
He brought in over 50 clinical psychiatrists
to try to see Michael, and each had different

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:44.740
opinions about him.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.480
During these 40 years, Michael rarely speaks,
which Sartain sees as a personal choice to

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.640
stay silent rather than a disability.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:54.230
In the years of Michael’s second stint of
captivity, Smith’s Grove Sanitarium became

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.700
Smith’s Grove State Hospital.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:59.490
Patients are calmed with old jazz music on
vinyl records, a courtyard area is outfitted

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:03.340
to give them their own space to get some fresh
air and sunshine every day and Sartain meets

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.420
individually with patients to check in on
them on a morningly basis.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:10.130
After 40 years of not much progress, Michael
was set to be transferred to a new facility,

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:15.180
Glass Hill, and assigned a new doctor on October
30th, 2018, the 40 year mark from the date

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.753
of his first escape.

00:13:16.753 --> 00:13:20.749
(impact)

00:13:21.993 --> 00:13:25.850
(mysterious music)

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:29.890
There are not many visitors for Smith’s
Grove's most infamous resident, so Dr. Sartain

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:33.440
doesn’t have many opportunities to see how
Michael reacts to different people or different

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.180
environments.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.620
I imagine this feels quite limiting to him,
and speculate that when British investigative

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.800
journalists Aaron Korey and Dana Haines approached
him about speaking to Michael, he gleefully

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.880
accepted, with hopes of seeing a new side
of his mysterious long studied mental case.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:50.220
They were able to arrange a meeting just before
the transfer on October 29th, 2018.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.279
– And there he is.

00:13:53.279 --> 00:13:56.740
– When introduced to the reporters, Michael
ignores them, so in order to try to elicit

00:13:56.740 --> 00:14:01.320
a response, he brings out the William Shatner
mask that was worn during the 1978 rampage,

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.110
but it manages to aggravate just about every
other patient than the one it was intended for.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:08.790
The evening of the 30th, each of the transferring
patients were lined up and loaded into a caged

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.750
school bus outfitted by the Illinois Department
of Corrections.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.410
Curiously, Dr. Sartain sees him through to
the end, and tries to comfort him, something

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.940
that seems unnecessary given that Michael
is a well established sociopath.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.587
– Don’t worry Michael.

00:14:20.587 --> 00:14:22.050
I’ll be by your side.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:26.050
– He even fights to go with on the bus, arguing
that Myers is his patient until he’s been

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.800
delivered into someone else’s care.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.650
During the ride, the bus crashes into a ditch
on Marlowe Road.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:34.570
My theory is that Laurie was the one to drive
the bus off the road in hopes of killing Michael,

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:36.390
but things do not go according to plan.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:40.540
She’s very unstable, and we do see her in
her car overseeing the patient transfer, plus

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.563
she hardly seems to react when the accident
is reported in the news.

00:14:43.563 --> 00:14:47.670
Someone, presumably Michael after being freed
by Sartain, attacks and seriously injures

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:50.670
the guards and bus driver, allowing the patients
to escape into the night.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:54.550
I say this because Dr. Sartain previously
expressed frustration in the fact that so

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:58.480
many clinical psychiatrists had looked at
Michael, but only one, Dr. Loomis, had gotten

00:14:58.480 --> 00:14:59.712
to study him in the wild.

00:14:59.712 --> 00:15:02.840
When a father and son drive up and discover
the accident, they both end up getting out

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.340
of the car to look around.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.790
Michael brutally snapped the neck of the father
and stealthily stowed himself away in their

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:08.790
backseat.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.000
The kid encounters the injured guard, who
urges him to just run, leading me to believe

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.920
that Michael was in fact the one to attack
him, showing off the unstoppable power that

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.590
had faded into legend over the last 40 years.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:22.760
And that legend was playing out once more
because Michael takes out the kid by surprise-choking

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:26.650
him when he gets back into the vehicle, just
as he did with Annie in 1978.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:30.550
This also allows him to steal that vehicle,
like he did during that first escape.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:34.110
To continue with the tradition, his first
stop in Haddonfield is at the cemetery where

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:35.410
his sister, Judith is buried.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.720
He finds the reporters from the previous day
recording more content at the Judith Myers

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:42.330
gravesite and decides to follow them to the
gas station in order to get his mask back.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:46.040
While Aaron is not looking, Myers walks into
the mechanic’s shop, punches him out, and

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.040
steals his suit.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:50.281
He also bashes an additional employee’s
face in and pockets his teeth, so he can drop

00:15:50.281 --> 00:15:53.680
them over the bathroom stall that Dana is
using to scare the sh*t out of her.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.990
Pun kinda intended.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.180
Aaron realizes what’s happening just in
time before his partner is killed, but even

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.670
whacking Michael in the face with a crowbar
is not enough to save her, and both of their

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:04.620
lives are taken, allowing Michael to reclaim
his prized mask.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:08.800
He would only need one more item to finish
his iconic look, and he would waste no time

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.475
getting it.

00:16:09.475 --> 00:16:12.400
Because it’s Halloween night, he blends
in with the crowd in costume, allowing him

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.540
to fly under the radar.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.620
Just like in his last rampage, he bumps into
some little kids, but lets them go.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.890
Even though the one kid comes really close
to dropping an f-bomb.

00:16:19.804 --> 00:16:21.489
– Oof!

00:16:21.489 --> 00:16:23.589
– What the f-
– BOOOOOOM!
(explosion)

00:16:23.589 --> 00:16:27.330
– [Zac] He steals a hammer from the Elrods’ shed
and uses it against Mrs. Elrod so he can claim

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:28.330
her kitchen knife.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.150
And with that, the look is complete.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:34.210
After 13 Halloween films, I’ve come to appreciate
just how important Michael’s appearance

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.250
is when it comes to making him a scary antagonist.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.010
And where’s a good reason for that.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.690
It goes back to the root reason that we are
drawn to horror movies.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:41.690
Human psychology.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:45.500
Danny McBride was onto something when he described
what makes Michael scary to him.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.520
He noted the contrast between the horrible
acts Michael commits, and the lack of emotion

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.380
that he seems to have while committing them.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.990
This is called incongruent affect.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.400
The literal definition of this term is when
feelings, mood, or emotions do not match up.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:00.870
In psychology, incongruent affect is when
a patient’s feelings do not match their

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.570
appearance, or do not match what is appropriate
for the situation.

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:07.490
It’s fitting that the first costume we ever
see Michael in is the clown costume, because

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.189
clowns are the perfect example of incongruent
affect.

00:17:10.189 --> 00:17:13.069
Many people find them creepy because their
painted smiles give them the appearance of

00:17:13.069 --> 00:17:17.620
always being happy, even if they are not happy,
or the situation does not call for happiness.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:22.240
That’s why seeing a clown at the circus
probably isn’t so creepy, if done correctly,

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:25.189
because the circus is a happy place and the
clowns are trying to be funny.

00:17:25.189 --> 00:17:29.960
But seeing a clown in a sewer grate, stand
pipe or abandoned house is definitely creepy.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.250
That’s incongruent affect.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.780
It comes off as creepy because we, as humans,
are designed to socialize with other humans.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:39.409
Humans have traditionally lived in tribes
with other humans for safety, so socialization

00:17:39.409 --> 00:17:40.375
meant survival.

00:17:40.375 --> 00:17:44.090
As a result, our brains have evolved for millions
of years to get really good at picking up

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.090
on social cues.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.850
That’s why outlets look like a face.

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.980
That’s why cars look like a face.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:52.409
That’s why Iggy Pop’s torso looks like
it’s about to cry.

00:17:52.409 --> 00:17:56.100
We are hardwired to pick up human emotions
using only visual cues.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:18:00.570
When those cues don’t match what the person
is really feeling, or don’t match the situation,

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:03.454
we pick up on that too, because it tells us
that something is wrong.

00:18:03.454 --> 00:18:07.379
Perhaps it is a predator trying to deceive
us, or there is something wrong with the person,

00:18:07.379 --> 00:18:09.369
and we need to heal someone in our tribe.

00:18:09.369 --> 00:18:13.399
Seeing Michael slashing up victims, all with
a blank, expressionless stare is an example

00:18:13.399 --> 00:18:14.765
of incongruent affect.

00:18:14.765 --> 00:18:18.679
Other Halloween films which make Michael look
surprised or angry just don’t have the same

00:18:18.679 --> 00:18:19.354
effect.

00:18:19.354 --> 00:18:23.379
And that’s why it’s important for Michael
to recollect all of the pieces of his iconic look.

00:18:23.379 --> 00:18:25.500
Now that he has his knife, he’s got to test
it out!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.740
And he finds a suitable victim in the house
next door.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.220
This victim seems to be chosen at random,
but the next would be chosen to maintain a

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.809
tradition established in ‘78.

00:18:32.809 --> 00:18:36.999
His main targets that year were Haddonfield’s
teen babysitters, Annie and Laurie.

00:18:36.999 --> 00:18:41.320
This year he finds another babysitter, Vicky,
who is looking after a boy named Julian Morrisey.

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:44.480
Like any good urban legend, the story begins
to repeat itself.

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:47.880
Michael sneaks into the house and stares through
Julian’s bedroom door, but again, isn’t

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:48.929
concerned with killing kids.

00:18:48.929 --> 00:18:52.059
It just freaks Julian out and gets him to
run down the stairs for help.

00:18:52.611 --> 00:18:54.000
– Ghosts and goblins little buddy?

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.000
– Shut up Dave!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:55.863
I heard him breathing.

00:18:55.863 --> 00:18:56.916
And then I saw him!

00:18:56.916 --> 00:18:57.806
He’s in here.

00:18:57.806 --> 00:18:59.139
The boogeyman’s in this house!

00:18:59.139 --> 00:19:01.490
– Michael hides in the closet while the room
is vacated.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.690
Vicky goes up to investigate, but doesn’t
find him there, because she’s not taking

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.360
Julian’s warning very seriously.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.769
As she puts him back to bed, he asks her to
close the closet door, but she finds something

00:19:09.769 --> 00:19:11.015
is blocking it.

00:19:11.015 --> 00:19:12.351
(door jamb)

00:19:13.891 --> 00:19:15.431
(loud music and scream)

00:19:15.431 --> 00:19:19.360
Michael is undeterred by Vicky throwing a
chair at him so she rushes out of the room,

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:22.629
but slips on the hardwood floor in the hallway,
allowing him to drag her back into the room

00:19:22.629 --> 00:19:24.360
and bring the knife down on her.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:29.324
After taking her out, he cocks his head, something
we saw him do after killing Bob Simms 40 years prior.

00:19:29.324 --> 00:19:32.169
This moment is explained by the actor behind
the mask: Nick Castle.

00:19:32.169 --> 00:19:36.000
He plays Myers in the original Halloween and
in parts of Halloween (2018).

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.460
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
he reveals that director John Carpenter instructed

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.409
him to tilt his head like that on the spot.

00:19:41.409 --> 00:19:44.940
“I had no idea what he was trying to get
at until I saw the movie and I said, ‘Oh,

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:47.049
how cool, it looks like I’m admiring my
kill.’”

00:19:47.049 --> 00:19:50.330
Which makes sense when paired with the pin-up
model comparison I made in my Things You Missed

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.669
in Halloween video; it’s almost as if the
body pinned to the wall is seen as a piece

00:19:53.669 --> 00:19:55.860
of artwork that Michael is gawking at.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:59.510
As we discussed, Michael is a mental patient
and a creature of habit, which is why Castle

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:02.270
was instructed to perform the head tilt again
after killing Vicky.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.740
Or at least that’s how I see it.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.658
I’m willing to close the door on that mystery.

00:20:06.698 --> 00:20:07.243
(door slams)

00:20:07.243 --> 00:20:10.850
Actually, everything he does before leaving
the house is a callback to his Bob Simms kill.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:14.180
He covers Vicky’s body with a bedsheet,
the same disguise he used for himself, after

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:17.710
finishing Bob, and then his next victim is
Vicky’s boyfriend Dave, who he pins to the

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.860
wall with his knife, just as he did to Bob.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.619
Frank Hawkins, now a deputy in his sixties,
shows up to investigate the disturbance and

00:20:23.619 --> 00:20:26.970
finds Vicky, but Michael is hiding in a bedroom
on the opposite side of the house, looking

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.830
out the window through the reflection of this
mirror.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:33.059
He makes eye contact with Laurie, the once
17-year old girl who evaded him the last time

00:20:33.059 --> 00:20:34.059
he was free.

00:20:34.059 --> 00:20:37.960
Now, at 57, she’s more prepared, and fires
a shot in his direction, which might have

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.450
at least dealt a blow to his head if she had
realized she was looking through a mirror.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:44.429
Michael walks out of the house, drawing the
attention of Hawkins, but he cannot land a

00:20:44.429 --> 00:20:45.429
shot either.

00:20:45.429 --> 00:20:48.690
The discovery of Dave’s body distracts his
attention, so Michael is once again able to

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.900
walk out and disappear into the black of the
night.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:52.600
But this time is different.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:56.261
This time, Laurie spots him and fires a shot
through the left side of his back before he

00:20:56.261 --> 00:20:57.710
completely disappears.

00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:01.330
This is the first time that Laurie has turned
the tables on him and become the hunter rather

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:02.370
than the hunted.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:05.529
Only Loomis was previously able to scare Michael
away up to this point.

00:21:05.529 --> 00:21:09.249
He retreats, and manages to get away and take
cover within the fortress of the Elrod’s

00:21:09.249 --> 00:21:11.619
backyard, which is surrounded by high concrete
walls.

00:21:11.619 --> 00:21:14.957
But eventually, a new victim falls into his
lap.

00:21:16.679 --> 00:21:18.320
(impact)

00:21:22.115 --> 00:21:25.545
(ominous music)

00:21:25.545 --> 00:21:29.140
High school student Oscar Berlucchi is in
a vulnerable state after getting drunk and

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.049
rejected by his crush, and mistakes Michael
for Mr. Elrod.

00:21:32.049 --> 00:21:35.779
The yard is illuminated by these motion sensored
lights, but each time they go off, Michael

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:37.789
somehow manages to creep closer.

00:21:37.789 --> 00:21:40.220
– [Oscar] Hey, where’d you go man?

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.629
You’re acting really sketchy right now.

00:21:43.629 --> 00:21:47.169
– Logically, it doesn’t make sense that Michael
should be able to move without turning the

00:21:47.169 --> 00:21:50.799
lights back on while Oscar can’t, but if
there’s any ability that seems to be focused

00:21:50.799 --> 00:21:54.750
on the most in this version of Michael’s
character, it is his ability to disappear.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:58.909
Part of what makes him so scary and unique
is that despite being a huge immovable force,

00:21:58.909 --> 00:22:00.159
he’s incredibly sneaky.

00:22:00.159 --> 00:22:03.400
He could be waiting behind any corner or hiding
within any shadow.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:06.769
Ever since Laurie first spotted him outside
her classroom window, there are many instances

00:22:06.769 --> 00:22:09.559
where he’ll be there one moment, but gone
the next.

00:22:09.559 --> 00:22:12.960
Perhaps he really does have a power to move
without being seen, and this allows him to

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:16.389
get the best of Oscar and stick a knife in
his back before he’s able to climb over

00:22:16.389 --> 00:22:17.570
the Elrod’s fence.

00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:20.940
When Oscar’s crush Allyson Nelson comes
back after hearing the commotion, the lights

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.761
turn on again, and Michael comes out to greet
her.

00:22:26.197 --> 00:22:27.285
(screams)

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:31.639
She runs away and gets help from the police,
so Michael ends up going for a stroll.

00:22:31.639 --> 00:22:34.989
He’s spotted and reported on 11th Street,
near Saint Park, where he encounters a police

00:22:34.989 --> 00:22:37.510
SUV carrying Hawkins, Sartain and Allyson.

00:22:37.510 --> 00:22:40.200
Upon seeing the scourge of Haddonfield, Hawkins
floors it.

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:43.529
Michael continues to walk right towards the
vehicle until the point of impact, demonstrating

00:22:43.529 --> 00:22:46.369
the complete lack of fear he saw towards bodily
injury.

00:22:46.369 --> 00:22:49.759
Hawkins rams Michael with the vehicle, knocking
him to the sidewalk, where he’s temporarily

00:22:49.759 --> 00:22:50.759
knocked out.

00:22:50.759 --> 00:22:54.360
To this point, we’ve seen Michael get knocked
out a few times, all of them during the 1978

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:55.360
rampage.

00:22:55.360 --> 00:22:58.840
He goes down after getting his neck punctured,
after getting stabbed in the eye and chest,

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:01.100
and finally after getting shot off a balcony.

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:04.679
Each time this happens, he lays there until
he can regain the strength to continue his

00:23:04.679 --> 00:23:07.519
spree, something that I refer to as his “recharge
period”.

00:23:07.519 --> 00:23:12.269
This scene is the first time we see Michael
recharge in 2018, which represents a terrifying possibility.

00:23:12.269 --> 00:23:15.620
Earlier we saw him get shot in the chest and
continue walking like nothing happened.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:19.880
That fact it takes a hit from a 5,000 lb Chevrolet
to put him down means he may have become even

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:21.679
stronger during his years of captivity.

00:23:21.679 --> 00:23:24.690
Or, if we’re going by the theory that Laurie
would later suggest, each of his kills adds

00:23:24.690 --> 00:23:26.990
to his power.

00:23:28.355 --> 00:23:33.929
– The more he kills, the more transcends
into something else impossible to defeat.

00:23:33.929 --> 00:23:37.490
When I covered Michael’s history in the
original timeline, I discussed the possibility

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:41.080
that he has the capability to kind of bear
down and hold off the recharge for a little

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:42.489
bit in critical situations.

00:23:42.489 --> 00:23:45.149
It’s possible that this is what happened
here as well.

00:23:45.149 --> 00:23:49.564
After getting shot, he held off doing a recharge
until the vehicular impact knocked him out cold. 

00:23:49.564 --> 00:23:52.120
This is also the longest he’s ever been
sidelined for.

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:56.559
He’s out for 4 minutes and 45 seconds, more
than twice as long as his longest nap to this point.

00:23:56.559 --> 00:24:00.379
During this time, Deputy Hawkins is prepared
to shoot him in the head, but Dr. Sartain

00:24:00.379 --> 00:24:02.919
gets out to protect the subject of his life’s
research.

00:24:02.919 --> 00:24:06.460
When Hawkins refuses to stand down, Sartain
attacks him and drags Michael into the cabin

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:08.520
of the vehicle, where Allyson is currently
locked.

00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:11.909
He heads towards Laurie Strode’s house,
hoping to see a reunion between the two.

00:24:11.909 --> 00:24:16.399
– [Sartain] Michael’s pursuit of Laurie Strode could
be what keeps him alive.

00:24:16.399 --> 00:24:23.350
I would suspect the notion of being the predator
or the fear of becoming prey keeps both of

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:24.480
them alive.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:27.129
– Laurie had previously expressed a similar
sentiment about her rival.

00:24:27.811 --> 00:24:29.319
– He waited for this night.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.235
– He’s waited for me.

00:24:31.235 --> 00:24:34.889
I don’t know if her interpretation is accurate,
but if it is, the wait would not have to go

00:24:34.889 --> 00:24:36.190
on much longer.

00:24:36.190 --> 00:24:39.720
Michael comes to in the back of the cop car
and kicks through the partition hard enough

00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:41.379
to basically immobilize him.

00:24:41.379 --> 00:24:44.630
Keep in mind, these partitions are made of
steel and they’re literally designed to

00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:48.769
keep officers in the front seats safe from
whatever unruly criminals they’re arresting.

00:24:48.769 --> 00:24:52.149
The fact that Michael destroys this barrier
in one kick is insane.

00:24:52.149 --> 00:24:55.799
He drags his doctor out of the car, allowing
Allyson the chance to escape, but Michael

00:24:55.799 --> 00:24:59.070
doesn’t seem to mind, because he’s mostly
concerned with stomping Sartain’s face in.

00:24:59.070 --> 00:25:02.609
He crushes the man’s head with one hard
stomp, more evidence that the Shape has kept

00:25:02.609 --> 00:25:04.879
himself in shape; he’s not skipping leg
day.

00:25:04.879 --> 00:25:06.669
Yeah, take a good look at that one Mikey.

00:25:06.669 --> 00:25:10.269
He proceeds to make quick work of the two
cops on standby outside of Laurie’s house,

00:25:10.269 --> 00:25:13.399
one gets his throat slashed with the pen blade
acquired from Sartain and the other just straight

00:25:13.399 --> 00:25:15.250
up gets turned into a man o’lantern.

00:25:15.250 --> 00:25:17.379
No, not that kind of man o’lantern.

00:25:17.379 --> 00:25:19.440
This kind looks almost just as painful.

00:25:19.440 --> 00:25:23.429
Michael parks the cop car outside of Laurie’s
house and gets the attention of her son-in-law

00:25:23.429 --> 00:25:26.190
Ray, so he also gets whacked when Michael
chokes him with a chain.

00:25:26.190 --> 00:25:30.070
If we were to give this one a 1978 counterpart,
it would be to Lynda van der Klok, who gets

00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:33.509
strangled with a telephone cord and stored
in a closet, which is exactly where Michael

00:25:33.509 --> 00:25:34.249
leaves Ray.

00:25:34.249 --> 00:25:36.563
But first, he’s got to break into the house.

00:25:36.563 --> 00:25:38.512
(breaking glass)

00:25:38.512 --> 00:25:40.679
The surprising move nearly kills Laurie.

00:25:40.679 --> 00:25:43.850
It makes me think back to an earlier part
of the movie where police told citizens to

00:25:43.850 --> 00:25:45.220
stay inside and lock their doors.

00:25:45.220 --> 00:25:48.821
When Michael Myers is on the loose, there’s
really no reliable line of defense, because

00:25:48.821 --> 00:25:52.100
even Laurie’s fortress is not enough to
withstand Michael’s brute force.

00:25:52.100 --> 00:25:56.100
She’s able to raise her shotgun in his direction
and, perhaps in an effort to keep the blast

00:25:56.100 --> 00:26:00.000
away from his head, he grabs the end of the
barrel and gets two of his fingers blasted off.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.230
It happens very quickly, and obviously I have
to blur it so that the YouTube Boogeyman doesn’t

00:26:04.230 --> 00:26:07.489
come for me in the night, but you can see
right here, as he’s letting go, Michael

00:26:07.489 --> 00:26:09.809
is now down to three remaining fingers.

00:26:09.809 --> 00:26:12.850
This is a good time to talk about how Michael
handles injuries in this timeline.

00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:16.756
Obviously Michael is nearly invincible, there’s
only one way to kill him, and nothing else

00:26:16.756 --> 00:26:18.470
seems to affect him much.

00:26:18.470 --> 00:26:22.010
But it’s still possible for him to get scars,
and each of his major injuries throughout

00:26:22.010 --> 00:26:23.859
the story visibly leaves a mark on him.

00:26:23.859 --> 00:26:25.929
The first is when Laurie gets him with the
knitting needle.

00:26:25.929 --> 00:26:28.059
The scar can be seen on his neck at the hospital.

00:26:28.059 --> 00:26:30.109
Laurie also jabs his eye with a coat hanger.

00:26:30.109 --> 00:26:32.960
After the prisoner escape, you can spot a
quick glimpse of the eye, and it’s clouded

00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:35.669
over as if to suggest he has lost vision on
that side.

00:26:35.669 --> 00:26:37.669
He’s also stabbed and shot in the torso.

00:26:37.669 --> 00:26:41.179
We haven’t had the Halloween beach OVA yet,
but if we did ever see him shirtless, I’m

00:26:41.179 --> 00:26:42.859
sure those scars would show up as well.

00:26:42.859 --> 00:26:47.014
That’s what the Michael Myers fangirls had
in mind when they first heard the title: Halloween H20.

00:26:47.014 --> 00:26:50.250
But the point is, it probably would have been
smarter for him to just grab the end of the

00:26:50.250 --> 00:26:53.799
gun without covering the cap, because he is
permanently left with three fingers on his

00:26:53.799 --> 00:26:54.799
left hand.

00:26:54.799 --> 00:26:57.549
This handicap doesn’t really slow him down
too much, but it stands to reason that you

00:26:57.549 --> 00:27:01.419
could reduce him into a non-threat if you
eventually removed all of his limbs or something.

00:27:01.419 --> 00:27:05.169
This is contrary to the original timeline
and 20 year timeline, where he gets shot in

00:27:05.169 --> 00:27:09.049
both eyes and blown up, but he just seems
to regenerate and eventually he looks fine.

00:27:09.049 --> 00:27:12.609
The setback doesn’t stop him from breaking
into the house as Laurie retreats to the basement

00:27:12.609 --> 00:27:14.409
to shoot up at him through the floorboards.

00:27:14.409 --> 00:27:18.260
Instead of going straight for her, he takes
this time to put away Ray’s body, as I mentioned earlier.

00:27:18.260 --> 00:27:20.880
He may not be a nice guy, but at least he
keeps things tidy.

00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:24.289
Laurie searches the house for him and finds
him in an upstairs bedroom, nearly identical

00:27:24.289 --> 00:27:26.269
to the one they fought in 40 years ago.

00:27:26.269 --> 00:27:30.859
But for the second time now, she is the aggressor,
and as Dr. Sartain predicted, they are both

00:27:30.859 --> 00:27:32.590
vying for that role of the predator.

00:27:32.590 --> 00:27:36.661
In ‘78, Michael came after her with a knife,
but she was eventually able to use it against him.

00:27:36.661 --> 00:27:40.600
Now Laurie is the one armed with a knife,
but it is Michael who finds a way to use it

00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:41.769
against her.

00:27:42.289 --> 00:27:43.590
(Laurie grunts)

00:27:43.590 --> 00:27:45.039
She also bites his hand,

00:27:45.039 --> 00:27:47.200
– Laurie Strode got hungry.

00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:51.320
– But this time, Laurie is the one to get thrown
off the balcony, so Michael turns his attention

00:27:51.320 --> 00:27:53.285
to her teenage granddaughter.

00:27:53.598 --> 00:27:55.598
(door hinges squeak)

00:27:58.126 --> 00:28:00.663
(impact)

00:28:03.167 --> 00:28:06.889
(somber music)

00:28:06.889 --> 00:28:11.570
– Allyson comes home, hoping to find safety
in her grandmother’s protection, but Michael

00:28:11.570 --> 00:28:13.109
hears her come in first.

00:28:13.109 --> 00:28:16.770
However, this brief distraction gives Laurie
enough time to pull another trick out of Michael’s

00:28:16.770 --> 00:28:18.169
book and disappear.

00:28:18.169 --> 00:28:21.769
He heads downstairs to try to finish off Laurie’s
bloodline, who are hiding in the basement.

00:28:21.769 --> 00:28:25.454
Laurie’s daughter, Karen, begs her mom
to come help her, but it’s a trap.

00:28:25.454 --> 00:28:26.227
– Gotcha.

00:28:26.433 --> 00:28:27.169
(gunshot)

00:28:27.169 --> 00:28:28.289
– In the face!

00:28:28.419 --> 00:28:31.580
– Laurie uses this opportunity to emerge from
the shadows and attack!

00:28:31.580 --> 00:28:34.350
Michael does land a blow against her with
a fire poker, but the tussle ends with her

00:28:34.350 --> 00:28:36.859
grabbing a frying pan to knock him down into
the basement.

00:28:36.859 --> 00:28:39.711
This triggers the second recharge period of
the night.

00:28:39.711 --> 00:28:42.950
It’s only a few seconds, but that’s just
enough for Allyson and Karen to climb to safety

00:28:42.950 --> 00:28:45.270
and shut the bars over the only exit.

00:28:45.270 --> 00:28:48.119
Michael finds himself in a basement sized
cage of Laurie’s design.

00:28:48.119 --> 00:28:51.499
She’s turning out to be a much more formidable
rival than he remembers her.

00:28:51.499 --> 00:28:55.200
She opens the gas valves throughout the house
and all he can do is stare as she tosses a

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:58.919
flare down into the basement, to ignite a
blaze on the man that haunted her nightmares

00:28:58.919 --> 00:29:00.710
for her entire adult life.

00:29:00.710 --> 00:29:05.549
Still, Michael is unflinching as the room
explodes around him, his empty eyes locked

00:29:05.549 --> 00:29:08.549
onto her just as they were since the very
beginning.

00:29:08.549 --> 00:29:12.961
One of the benefits of living in a small town
is that it doesn’t take long for the fire department to arrive.

00:29:12.961 --> 00:29:14.879
At least, it’s usually a benefit.

00:29:14.879 --> 00:29:18.659
One of Haddonfield’s finest falls through
the floorboards into the seemingly empty basement.

00:29:18.659 --> 00:29:23.330
Like a spider with a fly in its web, Laurie’s
gun closet opens to reveal Michael Myers.

00:29:23.330 --> 00:29:27.020
He brutally uses the firefighter’s own Halligan
bar against him, shattering his protective

00:29:27.020 --> 00:29:28.049
mask and face.

00:29:28.049 --> 00:29:31.630
His mayday call sends another firefighter
on the way to offer a hand of rescue, but

00:29:31.630 --> 00:29:34.470
Michael emerges from the smoke to yank him
into the basement as well.

00:29:34.470 --> 00:29:37.799
The efforts of the emergency crew, combined
with the collapsing structure of the house

00:29:37.799 --> 00:29:40.879
create a path of escape, and a shape appears
at the doorway.

00:29:40.879 --> 00:29:45.129
It’s *The* Shape, charred from the trap
Laurie had left him to die in, but stoic as

00:29:45.129 --> 00:29:48.620
ever as he clasps his new weapon with the
8 fingers he has left.

00:29:48.620 --> 00:29:52.620
The group of firefighters is well equipped
to fight back with axes, circle saws, and

00:29:52.620 --> 00:29:56.879
the power of numbers on their side, but Michael
Myers methodically destroys each of them.

00:29:56.879 --> 00:29:58.470
All in all, Michael tears through eleven men.

00:29:58.470 --> 00:29:59.470
– Eleven dead bodies.

00:29:59.470 --> 00:30:00.970
They’re all first responders.

00:30:00.970 --> 00:30:04.529
– Perhaps it is as the young Tommy Doyle suggested
so many years ago.

00:30:04.529 --> 00:30:07.429
– You can’t kill the Boogeyman.

00:30:07.429 --> 00:30:11.150
– But as I discussed, he’s not immune to injury,
and he’s still nursing that left hand.

00:30:11.150 --> 00:30:14.710
He sneaks into the home of Phil and Sondra
Larson, and raids their bathroom for first

00:30:14.710 --> 00:30:15.710
aid supplies.

00:30:15.710 --> 00:30:19.539
A small drone crash lands in the bathroom,
and probably not knowing what it is, he throws

00:30:19.539 --> 00:30:22.950
it out into the living room, getting the attention
of the terrified homeowners.

00:30:22.950 --> 00:30:26.539
When Phil comes in and turns the lights on,
he briefly sees Michael, with disinfectant,

00:30:26.539 --> 00:30:29.639
a soiled washcloth and bandages spread out
across the sink.

00:30:29.639 --> 00:30:32.919
Michael immediately smashes the light, and
Phil locks the door, but Michael powers his

00:30:32.919 --> 00:30:36.590
way through a glass window and bludgeons him
against the wall before pulling him down through

00:30:36.590 --> 00:30:38.359
the glass shards which puncture his neck.

00:30:38.359 --> 00:30:42.009
He does this all almost entirely with his
good hand, only bringing his bandaged hand

00:30:42.009 --> 00:30:45.570
up at the end to help grip Phil’s head;
he is quickly learning how to be resourceful

00:30:45.570 --> 00:30:47.029
with his remaining fingers.

00:30:47.029 --> 00:30:50.529
Sondra takes hold of a small kitchen knife
to defend herself, but Michael has another

00:30:50.529 --> 00:30:52.989
idea, and dismounts the fluorescent tube light
from above the stove.

00:30:52.989 --> 00:30:54.232
(glass shatters)

00:30:54.232 --> 00:30:56.232
(screaming and sobbing)

00:30:56.539 --> 00:30:58.639
He sticks it right though her neck and twists.

00:30:58.639 --> 00:31:02.139
Before leaving the house, Michael tosses Phil’s
still not dead body onto the table in the

00:31:02.139 --> 00:31:05.629
kitchen and sticks knife after knife after
knife into him, until he finally finds one

00:31:05.629 --> 00:31:07.659
he likes, and walks outside.

00:31:07.659 --> 00:31:11.389
Having taped up his hand and having acquired
a new knife, Michael makes his way home, but

00:31:11.389 --> 00:31:13.169
he would have to go across town to get there.

00:31:13.169 --> 00:31:17.112
He wanders the streets of Haddonfield as the
clock rolls over into the early hours of November

00:31:17.112 --> 00:31:18.470
1st, 2018.

00:31:18.470 --> 00:31:21.739
He goes through a park, where he is reportedly
up to his usual stalking antics.

00:31:22.356 --> 00:31:23.646
– [Lindsey] Where did you see him?

00:31:23.646 --> 00:31:24.926
– He’s just hiding behind trees.

00:31:24.926 --> 00:31:26.109
– And he pops out, I’m like, peek-a-boo!

00:31:26.109 --> 00:31:27.724
I mean we’re not 3 years old.

00:31:27.724 --> 00:31:28.659
Come on man!

00:31:28.659 --> 00:31:31.889
– When one of the kids wanders from the group,
Michael gets him without the others noticing.

00:31:31.889 --> 00:31:35.239
We don’t see it, but we do see the kid’s
mask, dripping in the aftermath.

00:31:35.239 --> 00:31:39.539
These kids appear to be young teenagers, maybe
13, so I’m guessing Michael really does

00:31:39.539 --> 00:31:43.570
draw the line, regarding who he’s willing
to kill, between teenagers and pre-teens.

00:31:43.570 --> 00:31:46.690
He spots another face from his past talking
to the other 2 teens.

00:31:46.690 --> 00:31:49.919
This is Lindsey Wallace, the same girl that
Annie was babysitting before being killed

00:31:49.919 --> 00:31:51.929
by Michael 480 months before.

00:31:52.319 --> 00:31:53.259
That’s 40 years.

00:31:53.259 --> 00:31:56.070
I just wanted to change things up, because
I feel like I keep saying that.

00:31:56.070 --> 00:32:00.229
He also discovers an SUV containing Marion
Chambers and two other passengers.

00:32:00.229 --> 00:32:04.249
Mimicking what he did to her in 1978, he climbs
on top of the vehicle and grabs her through

00:32:04.249 --> 00:32:07.049
the window, but this time she’s armed and
tries to shoot at him through the roof.

00:32:07.049 --> 00:32:10.445
When he comes down to meet her face to face,
she’s got a line prepared for him.

00:32:10.445 --> 00:32:12.389
– Hey Michael!

00:32:12.389 --> 00:32:13.799
This is for Dr. Loomis.

00:32:13.799 --> 00:32:16.259
– Ah yes, let’s avenge Dr. Loomis.

00:32:16.259 --> 00:32:19.139
The one guy who seemingly died of natural
causes in this timeline.

00:32:19.139 --> 00:32:22.690
Fortunately for Michael, her tribute to her
former colleague doesn’t work out, because

00:32:22.690 --> 00:32:23.729
she’s out of bullets.

00:32:23.729 --> 00:32:27.989
(Marion clicking gun and babbling in fear)

00:32:27.989 --> 00:32:31.690
He climbs into the window and stabs her four
times before he’s strangled with a prop

00:32:31.690 --> 00:32:33.779
stethoscope by the man in the backseat.

00:32:33.779 --> 00:32:37.070
Michael is not affected by this at all, and
sticks the knife into the man’s left eye,

00:32:37.070 --> 00:32:38.539
putting an end to the struggle.

00:32:38.539 --> 00:32:40.159
Maybe Michael picked that one up from Laurie
Strode.

00:32:40.159 --> 00:32:43.590
The man’s wife comes back towards the vehicle
with a handgun, and Michael’s quick thinking

00:32:43.590 --> 00:32:48.000
results in a kill that would probably be more
at home in an FPS montage than a Halloween movie.

00:32:49.549 --> 00:32:51.145
(airhorns and cheering)

00:32:51.145 --> 00:32:55.369
As Michael does his trademark corpse admiration
head tilt, he gets a surprise bag of bricks

00:32:55.369 --> 00:32:56.869
to the face from Lindsey.

00:32:56.869 --> 00:33:00.710
Despite being one of the four survivors of
the babysitter murders, she vastly underestimates

00:33:00.710 --> 00:33:02.450
him, and he chokeslams her against the car.

00:33:02.450 --> 00:33:06.080
However, her experience does help her, because
she’s able to use the same tactic that Laurie

00:33:06.080 --> 00:33:09.509
once used to get away from his grip, by removing
The Boogeyman’s mask.

00:33:09.509 --> 00:33:13.330
After readjusting it, he follows her into
the woods at his customary walking pace.

00:33:13.330 --> 00:33:17.309
We are now moving at the speed of… pretty
slow but somehow intimidating.

00:33:17.309 --> 00:33:21.419
Shortly thereafter, the couple from the SUV
is somehow moved to the carousel at the park,

00:33:21.419 --> 00:33:24.850
and Marion is decorated with the Witch mask
left behind by the teens and hung from the

00:33:24.850 --> 00:33:25.989
top of the swingset.

00:33:25.989 --> 00:33:29.480
We literally see Michael leave the scene to
look for Lindsey, so the only explanation

00:33:29.480 --> 00:33:31.649
is that he went back to rearrange the bodies.

00:33:31.649 --> 00:33:34.289
Which, to be fair, is consistent with his
character.

00:33:34.289 --> 00:33:38.419
Annie, Lynda and Bob were arranged in a scene
in ‘78, and he also pays special attention

00:33:38.419 --> 00:33:42.148
to the presentation of Vicky and Ray earlier
on this night in 2018.

00:33:42.148 --> 00:33:46.099
Seeing this trend repeated so many times makes
me automatically start searching for a reason

00:33:46.099 --> 00:33:46.774
behind it.

00:33:46.774 --> 00:33:50.471
As with many aspects of the character, we’ll
probably never get a definitive answer, so

00:33:50.471 --> 00:33:52.999
all I can do is use the clues and speculate.

00:33:52.999 --> 00:33:56.599
The first scene was clearly a recreation of
his sister’s grave site, which is something

00:33:56.599 --> 00:34:00.680
that happened when Michael was a kid, and
this one depicts the bodies playing at a playground,

00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:02.659
somewhere you would usually find kids.

00:34:02.659 --> 00:34:06.919
Michael was a child during his first killing,
and we know he has psychological issues -- he’s

00:34:06.919 --> 00:34:09.250
been in a mental hospital for 55 years.

00:34:09.250 --> 00:34:13.280
Maybe his childhood trauma prevented him from
maturing out of a childlike mindset.

00:34:13.280 --> 00:34:17.000
Maybe he sees these bodies as toys that he
can play with and maybe he avoids killing

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:19.960
kids because he sees them as one of his own
kind.

00:34:19.960 --> 00:34:22.800
His next destination would also play into
this idea.

00:34:22.800 --> 00:34:26.280
Because Michael Myers would return to his
childhood home.

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:28.232
(impact)

00:34:30.970 --> 00:34:34.420
(mellow music)

00:34:34.420 --> 00:34:38.190
The first time Michael broke out of Smith’s
Grove, he visited his former residence and

00:34:38.190 --> 00:34:39.190
found it abandoned.

00:34:39.190 --> 00:34:43.580
It was in a dilapidated state, but other than
the natural effects of time, it was unaltered.

00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:45.840
This time, the property no longer sat empty.

00:34:45.840 --> 00:34:48.990
He would find it occupied by two men: Big
John and Little John.

00:34:48.990 --> 00:34:52.350
He sneaks in through the back door, probably
because this was the entrance he used shortly

00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:53.350
before killing Judith.

00:34:53.350 --> 00:34:57.360
I also find it interesting that he leaves
behind a three fingered handprint on the doorframe.

00:34:57.360 --> 00:35:01.230
It almost looks like a dinosaur track, which
seems appropriate given Tommy’s speech at

00:35:01.230 --> 00:35:02.300
the hospital.

00:35:02.300 --> 00:35:04.110
– He is an apex predator!

00:35:04.110 --> 00:35:08.760
– The way Dr. Sartain describes him compares
him to another apex predator, a shark.

00:35:10.125 --> 00:35:13.100
– He only knows how to keep moving and keep
killing.

00:35:13.100 --> 00:35:15.960
And he will kill again unless he’s captured.

00:35:15.960 --> 00:35:17.520
– This is actually no mistake.

00:35:17.520 --> 00:35:21.440
In an interview with HalloweenMovies.com,
director David Gordon-Green explains how he

00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:24.680
used Jaws, almost like a template for this
iteration of Michael Myers.

00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:26.910
“In some ways, it's like a film like Jaws.

00:35:26.910 --> 00:35:28.970
There's not a lot of personality in the shark.

00:35:28.970 --> 00:35:32.410
Technically he's very elusive and we're trying
to keep that as our framework and not get

00:35:32.410 --> 00:35:35.580
too much into who he is, why he is, or what
he's been doing.”

00:35:35.580 --> 00:35:39.240
It sounds like this approach was also communicated
to mask designer Christopher Nelson.

00:35:39.240 --> 00:35:44.490
– [Nelson] And it ended up being this very
strange mannequin-like soulless, almost Great

00:35:44.490 --> 00:35:46.080
white shark of a human.

00:35:46.080 --> 00:35:50.588
– In this scenario, much like the opening scene
of Jaws, the predator stalks its prey silently.

00:35:50.588 --> 00:35:54.510
Michael sneaks around upstairs and gets the
draw on Big John without ever being noticed.

00:35:54.510 --> 00:35:57.160
And squeezes his eyes out of their sockets
just for good measure.

00:35:57.160 --> 00:36:00.673
After this, Michael resumes the position he
took as a child, just staring out his sister’s

00:36:00.673 --> 00:36:01.673
bedroom window.

00:36:01.673 --> 00:36:04.030
When Little John addresses him, he turns and
approaches.

00:36:04.030 --> 00:36:07.085
It is not long before he joins his partner
in death.

00:36:07.085 --> 00:36:09.015
– [Little John] Noooo!!!

00:36:09.015 --> 00:36:12.480
– He poses the remains of the two Johns just
like a photo found in their study, only their

00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:13.480
positions are switched.

00:36:13.480 --> 00:36:16.610
I don’t have time to explain the significance
of that here, but watch my Things You Missed

00:36:16.610 --> 00:36:19.110
in Halloween Kills after this if you’re
interested.

00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:22.050
Another trait of Michael’s that we’ve
seen come up time and time again is his love

00:36:22.050 --> 00:36:23.050
of darkness.

00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:24.700
There’s one I can relate to.

00:36:24.700 --> 00:36:28.780
We saw him turn off all the lights after taking
over the Wallace house in 1978, and he follows

00:36:28.780 --> 00:36:31.240
suit here after reclaiming his own residence.

00:36:31.240 --> 00:36:34.290
This makes it easier for him to hide in the
shadows and hunt his prey.

00:36:34.290 --> 00:36:37.890
The next victim is Lonnie Elam, the kid that
Michael briefly encountered just outside the

00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:40.310
Myers house after escaping from Dr. Loomis.

00:36:40.310 --> 00:36:43.220
Now that he’s no longer a kid, he’s a
perfectly viable target.

00:36:43.220 --> 00:36:46.630
He makes quick work of Lonnie and throws him
into the attic, then hides in a closet and

00:36:46.630 --> 00:36:48.300
waits for someone to come looking for him.

00:36:48.300 --> 00:36:51.000
And that someone is Lonnie’s teenage son
Cameron.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.850
Michael bursts out of the closet and pins
him to the wall where he is able to stab him

00:36:53.850 --> 00:36:54.850
several times.

00:36:54.850 --> 00:36:58.630
Cameron’s girlfriend, Allyson, comes marching
with a shotgun, which he easily deflects,

00:36:58.630 --> 00:37:02.020
but she’s able to land several knife jabs
into his stomach before he slams her face

00:37:02.020 --> 00:37:04.300
into a railing and tosses her down the stairs.

00:37:04.300 --> 00:37:07.750
As he finishes Cameron, Allyson challenges
him to come get her, in hopes of creating

00:37:07.750 --> 00:37:13.220
a distraction, but he doesn't come for her until after breaking Cameron’s
neck with a 180° twist.

00:37:13.220 --> 00:37:17.690
Allyson is nowhere near a match for Michael’s
quick reflexes and strength, but she’s saved

00:37:17.690 --> 00:37:20.750
when her mom shows up to save the day by stabbing
Michael in the back with the pitchfork 

00:37:20.750 --> 00:37:21.980
found on the front porch.

00:37:21.980 --> 00:37:24.970
This is actually one of the most effective
attacks that we’ve ever seen against him,

00:37:24.970 --> 00:37:28.710
he actually appears to recoil in pain for
a moment as he’s driven to the ground.

00:37:28.710 --> 00:37:32.760
What makes this pitchfork so effective as
opposed to the stabs and gunshots he’s endured

00:37:32.760 --> 00:37:34.040
all night long?

00:37:34.040 --> 00:37:36.880
In my opinion, this goes back to the recharge
period.

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:38.295
Imagine Michael is like a Pokémon,

00:37:38.295 --> 00:37:39.790
just hang with me for a second here!

00:37:39.790 --> 00:37:41.460
He has a set amount of Health Points.

00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:45.580
Each attack against him will lower his HP,
but they won’t slow him down until his bar

00:37:45.580 --> 00:37:46.630
reaches zero.

00:37:46.630 --> 00:37:50.420
Once that happens, he faints and has to rest
for a little while before his health is restored,

00:37:50.420 --> 00:37:52.230
at which point he can go on fighting again.

00:37:52.230 --> 00:37:55.450
You can make him faint all you want, but that
doesn’t mean he’s going to die.

00:37:55.450 --> 00:37:57.085
He’s not Gary’s Raticate.

00:37:57.085 --> 00:37:59.000
(Lavender Town syndrome music)

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:03.680
So the pitchfork, and the subsequent head
stomp was probably just the final blow, the

00:38:03.680 --> 00:38:05.270
last of Michael’s HP.

00:38:05.270 --> 00:38:08.960
This recharge period is pretty short though,
just long enough for Karen to steal Michael’s

00:38:08.960 --> 00:38:12.530
mask, which tracks now as a well tested method
to distract him from anything else.

00:38:12.530 --> 00:38:16.750
He totally ignores the vulnerable Allyson
and walks after Karen, who goads him on, through

00:38:16.750 --> 00:38:21.170
backyards and side yards, into another
street, which turns out to be yet another trap. 

00:38:21.170 --> 00:38:25.650
He’s surrounded by an angry mob of Haddonfield
townspeople and their obnoxiously big trucks.

00:38:25.650 --> 00:38:26.650
F*ck cars.

00:38:26.650 --> 00:38:30.490
They’re led by Leigh Brackett, the father
of the babysitter Annie, whose life he famously

00:38:30.490 --> 00:38:34.620
cut short 40 years before, and by Tommy Doyle,
the boy that Laurie was babysitting during

00:38:34.620 --> 00:38:36.820
her encounter with Michael that same night.

00:38:36.820 --> 00:38:41.610
The mob is armed with firearms, hockey sticks,
shovels, pipes, baseball bats, and one lady

00:38:41.610 --> 00:38:42.610
even brings an iron.

00:38:42.610 --> 00:38:45.400
Not a golf club, but like a clothing iron,
for some reason.

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:49.030
With Michael surrounded, they’re able to
overwhelm him by attacking from his blind

00:38:49.030 --> 00:38:52.810
side, burying close range shots into him and
turning up the beatdown once he hits the pavement.

00:38:52.810 --> 00:38:56.930
He drops his knife, and barely has the strength
to reach for it, so Karen, the woman whose

00:38:56.930 --> 00:39:01.530
life was spent preparing for Michael’s onslaught,
grabs it and slashes it into his upper back.

00:39:01.530 --> 00:39:05.560
It looks like it may be over for Michael,
that he had finally met his match.

00:39:05.560 --> 00:39:09.730
Just to be sure, Brackett lines up his gun
to Myers head, but in one quick motion, the

00:39:09.730 --> 00:39:14.032
evil being draws the knife from his own back
and uses it to slash through Brackett’s throat.

00:39:14.032 --> 00:39:16.600
From here, Michael’s abilities seem to grow.

00:39:16.600 --> 00:39:20.240
Laurie Strode has the theory about Michael’s
tendency to seemingly become more and more

00:39:20.240 --> 00:39:21.550
difficult to defeat.

00:39:21.550 --> 00:39:25.560
She believes that the more he kills, the more
transcends into something else impossible

00:39:25.560 --> 00:39:26.560
to take down.

00:39:26.560 --> 00:39:29.830
I guess my Pokémon analogy is actually perfect
to describe this too.

00:39:29.830 --> 00:39:33.900
In Pokémon, the more monsters you defeat,
the more experience you gain, which eventually

00:39:33.900 --> 00:39:34.900
levels you up.

00:39:34.900 --> 00:39:38.380
After taking out Leigh Brackett, Michael seems
to get a boost in his abilities, and the same

00:39:38.380 --> 00:39:43.090
attackers he was overwhelmed by moments earlier
are now outmaneuvered, overpowered, and with

00:39:43.090 --> 00:39:46.260
a little bit of luck… come on people of
Haddonfield, you gotta learn to keep track

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:50.300
of how much ammunition you have left… he
takes each of them down until it’s just

00:39:50.300 --> 00:39:51.300
him and Tommy.

00:39:51.300 --> 00:39:54.160
When Michael deals the finishing blow, the
two lock eyes…

00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:55.160
sort of.

00:39:55.160 --> 00:39:59.320
Michael looks into Tommy’s eyes but Tommy
can only see the dark voids of shadow created

00:39:59.320 --> 00:40:00.320
by the mask.

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:03.740
When covered by the mask under the fall of
night, the facial features that make him human

00:40:03.740 --> 00:40:07.500
just aren’t visible, another example of
incongruent affect.

00:40:07.500 --> 00:40:11.470
With the entire mob taken care of, Michael
returns to his post, sneaking past the commotion

00:40:11.470 --> 00:40:15.550
of emergency vehicles and crime scene investigators
to return to Judith’s old bedroom.

00:40:15.550 --> 00:40:19.600
He finds Karen, standing at his spot, gazing
out the window, but by the time she notices

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:22.050
him in the reflection, it’s already too
late for her.

00:40:22.050 --> 00:40:26.839
Karen is killed, and The Shape retakes his
rightful place atop Haddonfield.

00:40:28.983 --> 00:40:32.340
– [Dr Sartain] How does a crime like Michael's
affect him?

00:40:32.340 --> 00:40:34.790
What's that feeling?

00:40:34.790 --> 00:40:38.530
Is he on a random path or is he emotionally
driven?

00:40:38.530 --> 00:40:39.975
Triggered by something.

00:40:39.975 --> 00:40:44.300
Perhaps some unheard marching order imprinted on his
very being?

00:40:44.300 --> 00:40:46.625
I want to know what he’s feeling.

00:40:46.625 --> 00:40:49.615
I want to know what pleasure he gets out of killing.

00:40:49.615 --> 00:40:54.740
– Dr. Sartain, in his quest to understand the
mind of a killer, nearly became a killer himself.

00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:58.300
He wanted to gain more insight into Michael
by observing him in the wild.

00:40:58.300 --> 00:41:02.430
As misguided as this may have been, could
it be argued that seeing Michael break free

00:41:02.430 --> 00:41:04.970
for a third time helps us understand him?

00:41:04.970 --> 00:41:06.740
Helps us identify his patterns?

00:41:06.740 --> 00:41:08.785
Helps us understand the mind of a killer?

00:41:08.785 --> 00:41:09.525
Maybe.

00:41:09.525 --> 00:41:13.850
It’s up to your interpretation if any of
the analysis provided in this video, or any

00:41:13.850 --> 00:41:18.020
of your own conclusions hold any more ground
than any of the 50 psychiatrists who examined

00:41:18.020 --> 00:41:19.060
him in captivity.

00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:23.010
Personally, to this point, I feel pretty good
about all of my teachings here in this lesson,

00:41:23.010 --> 00:41:25.530
but I’d still hesitate to call them definitive.

00:41:25.530 --> 00:41:27.650
Mostly because of what happens next.

00:41:27.650 --> 00:41:30.170
Just when we think we’re starting to understand
Michael…

00:41:30.170 --> 00:41:31.610
the pattern breaks.

00:41:31.610 --> 00:41:34.160
He doesn’t go back into captivity as you
would expect.

00:41:34.160 --> 00:41:36.683
This time, Michael gets away.

00:41:36.683 --> 00:41:40.558
(impact)

00:41:41.644 --> 00:41:45.335
(mysterious music)

00:41:45.335 --> 00:41:49.310
“A manhunt for suspected killer Michael
Myers continues in Haddonfield, Illinois on

00:41:49.310 --> 00:41:52.850
Friday, two days after 27 people were brutally
killed on Halloween night.

00:41:52.850 --> 00:41:57.325
The suspect, Michael Myers, 61, is believed
to have fled the area and is currently at large. 

00:41:57.325 --> 00:42:00.660
He is in possession of a knife and considered
armed and very dangerous.”

00:42:00.660 --> 00:42:04.680
That’s what newspapers read in early November
after Michael Myers's worst crime spree yet.

00:42:04.680 --> 00:42:06.590
However, they were wrong about two things.

00:42:06.590 --> 00:42:08.200
The first being Michael’s kill count.

00:42:08.200 --> 00:42:11.610
They probably haven’t even tallied all the
bodies, yet, because it’s more like 57,

00:42:11.610 --> 00:42:14.640
give or take a few whose fate is never explicitly
seen.

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:17.610
The second error is that Michael did not necessarily
leave the area.

00:42:17.610 --> 00:42:21.200
At this time, he most likely retreated to
the sewers where he could easily lay low while

00:42:21.200 --> 00:42:22.320
the drama died down.

00:42:22.320 --> 00:42:26.320
I imagine at some point he tried to go back
home, but found his old residence demolished,

00:42:26.320 --> 00:42:28.160
and ended up just staying in the sewer.

00:42:28.160 --> 00:42:31.650
Over the next 4 years, there were other Halloween
murders, which were ultimately determined

00:42:31.650 --> 00:42:34.380
to be inspired by Michael, but not committed
by Michael himself.

00:42:34.380 --> 00:42:38.700
There were also people who went missing around
Halloween and never turned up, like Meagan

00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:40.680
Baxter, in October 2021.

00:42:40.680 --> 00:42:43.560
Despite the fact that police did not name
Michael Myers as the culprit for any of this,

00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:47.280
it is likely that he did take in a few victims
during this time, based on the comments of

00:42:47.280 --> 00:42:49.690
this homeless man who hangs out around the
sewer entrance.

00:42:49.690 --> 00:42:52.510
– You see that man in there?

00:42:52.510 --> 00:42:56.280
He’ll take people in there now and then.

00:42:56.280 --> 00:42:58.630
Why’d he let you live?

00:42:58.630 --> 00:43:02.450
– We have no way of knowing which victims were taken by
Michael, and which were taken by other

00:43:02.450 --> 00:43:05.910
people, because the police seem like they
are just taking educated guesses rather than

00:43:05.910 --> 00:43:08.000
getting real evidence, for some reason.

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:11.152
– Do you think he's come back?
– Michael doesn’t use guns.

00:43:11.152 --> 00:43:12.830
I really don’t understand that logic.

00:43:12.830 --> 00:43:16.080
Just because Michael has not fired a gun in
the past doesn’t mean he isn’t going to.

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:19.040
He never killed anyone with a Halligan bar…
until he did.

00:43:19.040 --> 00:43:23.190
Plus, one of his victims did die from a gunshot,
even if he wasn’t the one to fire it.

00:43:23.190 --> 00:43:26.400
I’m guessing he mostly just killed people
near the sewer entrance though, in order to

00:43:26.400 --> 00:43:27.400
keep a lower profile.

00:43:27.400 --> 00:43:31.490
For example, Meagan Baxter’s missing billboard
is right near this overpass, and it makes

00:43:31.490 --> 00:43:35.080
sense that they would want to place this near
the location she was believed to have disappeared,

00:43:35.080 --> 00:43:37.040
so she was probably taken by Michael.

00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:42.310
In October 2022, a young man named Corey Cunningham
is tossed from the overpass into the hobo camp,

00:43:42.310 --> 00:43:45.260
where he is abducted by Michael, who drags
him into the sewers.

00:43:45.260 --> 00:43:47.670
Strangely he doesn’t kill Corey while he’s
passed out.

00:43:47.670 --> 00:43:51.870
As he tries to escape, Michael reaches out
and tries to strangle him, during which they

00:43:51.870 --> 00:43:55.930
make eye contact, and something seems to be
passed between the two, and Corey escapes.

00:43:55.930 --> 00:43:59.380
We’re not really given a reason that Michael
lets Corey live, but we are given a reason

00:43:59.380 --> 00:44:01.313
for Allyson’s attraction to Corey.

00:44:02.060 --> 00:44:07.070
– I know what it’s like to have everybody
looking at you thinking that they know you,

00:44:07.070 --> 00:44:09.790
thinking that they know what you’ve been
through, but they don’t.

00:44:09.790 --> 00:44:12.530
– So maybe Michael relates to Corey on a similar
level.

00:44:12.530 --> 00:44:16.461
Then on October 29th, Corey leads a police
officer named Doug Mulaney into the sewer

00:44:16.461 --> 00:44:18.370
where Michael is waiting for him.

00:44:18.370 --> 00:44:22.000
Michael jumps Officer Mulaney, but Mulaney
is able to get the upper hand and knock Michael

00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:23.000
to the floor.

00:44:23.000 --> 00:44:27.210
But Corey intervenes by attacking Mulaney,
and begs Michael to show him how he kills.

00:44:27.210 --> 00:44:30.700
Michael grabs a rusted old knife, probably
the same one from the Larsens’ house, and

00:44:30.700 --> 00:44:34.740
Corey restrains Mulaney, giving Michael the
opportunity to slash his throat and stab him

00:44:34.740 --> 00:44:35.820
over and over.

00:44:35.820 --> 00:44:39.830
We can see the life and power return to Michael’s
body as he does this, and he stabs Mulaney

00:44:39.830 --> 00:44:42.980
several times more each with increasing tempo
and power.

00:44:42.980 --> 00:44:46.660
It appears that Laurie’s theory is partially
correct, the more that Michael kills, the

00:44:46.660 --> 00:44:48.120
more powerful he becomes.

00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:51.350
However, at this point, he seems weaker than
he was in 2018.

00:44:51.350 --> 00:44:55.560
My first thought was that long periods without
killing can drain his power, however, that

00:44:55.560 --> 00:44:57.900
doesn’t exactly track with his escape four
years prior.

00:44:57.900 --> 00:45:01.920
He had not killed anyone during his 40 year
stay at Smith’s Grove, yet, he still had

00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:04.490
the power to overtake the entire bus full
of armed guards.

00:45:04.490 --> 00:45:08.401
So it could be that Michael’s power is fading
as he gets older, and he needs to continue

00:45:08.401 --> 00:45:10.570
to kill in order to maintain his strength.

00:45:10.570 --> 00:45:13.900
Another thought I’m stewing with is that
maybe killing is not what gives him power,

00:45:13.900 --> 00:45:16.890
but maybe his status as the boogeyman is what
gives him power.

00:45:16.890 --> 00:45:21.690
This would explain why his power builds through
1978, but Laurie, the one character who doesn’t

00:45:21.690 --> 00:45:23.105
believe in the Boogeyman, survives.

00:45:23.105 --> 00:45:26.290
Then in 2018, his notoriety had grown even
greater.

00:45:26.290 --> 00:45:30.480
We literally see reporters coming to Haddonfield
from across the globe to investigate him.

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:34.300
With each victim he took that year, he became
even more infamous, which makes it appear

00:45:34.300 --> 00:45:36.660
as if each kill is actually powering him up.

00:45:36.660 --> 00:45:40.800
But then in 2019, Corey Cunningham killed
the kid he was babysitting and he became the

00:45:40.800 --> 00:45:42.540
new villain of Haddonfield.

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:46.825
Michael was now sharing the boogeyman spotlight,
and some of that power went to Corey, not to Michael.

00:45:46.825 --> 00:45:49.270
– I keep seeing his eyes.

00:45:49.270 --> 00:45:50.810
Michael’s eyes.

00:45:50.810 --> 00:45:51.810
In Corey.

00:45:51.810 --> 00:45:55.390
– The one snag in this theory is that he kills
Officer Mulaney in private.

00:45:55.390 --> 00:45:59.170
Before the town learns about his death, we
see the power immediately go back to Michael.

00:45:59.170 --> 00:46:01.870
However, there is one witness to this: Corey.

00:46:01.870 --> 00:46:05.930
Even if he is just an audience of one, Michael
is still bringing life back into the urban

00:46:05.930 --> 00:46:08.940
legend, which in turns literally gives life
to the legend himself.

00:46:08.940 --> 00:46:12.160
It’s something I’ve brought up several
times throughout his history, so Michael’s

00:46:12.160 --> 00:46:15.310
status as an urban legend may be important
here as well.

00:46:15.310 --> 00:46:19.180
After this, Michael follows Corey, who goes
back to Laurie’s new house, where he witnesses

00:46:19.180 --> 00:46:23.900
the woman he’s become all too familiar with
over the last 44 years spying in her own windows,

00:46:23.900 --> 00:46:26.520
at a young couple, much like he did as a child.

00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:31.500
The next night he follows Corey again, this
time to the home of Dr. Mathis, Allyson’s ***hole boss.

00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:34.530
He watches as the young man in the scarecrow
mask takes him out.

00:46:34.530 --> 00:46:38.020
Corey is unable to reach Mathis’s girlfriend
before she locks him out of the house, but

00:46:38.020 --> 00:46:40.000
Michael is already there waiting for her.

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:43.730
He puts his full power on display for the
first time in four years by pinning her up

00:46:43.730 --> 00:46:47.415
against the wall with his knife, as he had
with Bob Simms and Dave in the past.

00:46:47.415 --> 00:46:50.620
Earlier I talked about Michael’s head tilt
being a sign that he is admiring his kill

00:46:50.620 --> 00:46:54.993
like artwork, and that idea is furthered here,
because Deborah is pinned up over a large painting.

00:46:54.993 --> 00:46:58.610
The next day is an important one: October
31st.

00:46:58.610 --> 00:47:02.750
Halloween fell upon Haddonfield once again,
and it would not pass without their infamous

00:47:02.750 --> 00:47:06.293
boogeyman paying them one final visit.

00:47:06.293 --> 00:47:09.659
(impact)

00:47:11.565 --> 00:47:15.085
(horror soundscape)
(dripping)

00:47:15.085 --> 00:47:19.720
Michael’s favorite holiday begins on a low
note, with Corey charging into the sewers,

00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:22.760
picking a fight with him, pinning him to the
ground and stealing his mask.

00:47:22.760 --> 00:47:26.000
As he does this, he says “you’re just
a man in a Halloween mask”.

00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:29.560
Perhaps he is able to overpower Michael because
of this belief that he’s nothing more than

00:47:29.560 --> 00:47:30.560
an ordinary man.

00:47:30.560 --> 00:47:32.573
He could not have been more wrong.

00:47:34.203 --> 00:47:38.190
As we’ve seen time and time again, Michael
will stop at nothing to get his mask back.

00:47:38.190 --> 00:47:41.500
He somehow tracks Corey to Laurie Strode’s
house and sneaks in through the back door

00:47:41.500 --> 00:47:43.380
to reclaim his mask once again.

00:47:43.380 --> 00:47:46.910
By the time Michael gets there, Corey appears
to be laying dead in the foyer, but when the

00:47:46.910 --> 00:47:50.490
Shape reaches down to take his knife, he springs
to life and grabs Michael’s hand.

00:47:50.490 --> 00:47:54.010
It would appear that Corey has just had his
own “recharge period”, but I’ll come

00:47:54.010 --> 00:47:55.370
back to that a little bit later.

00:47:55.370 --> 00:47:59.380
This time, Michael is the apex predator once
more, and he snaps Corey’s neck.

00:47:59.380 --> 00:48:03.280
Now he can turn his attention back to Laurie
Strode for one last showdown.

00:48:03.280 --> 00:48:06.490
He goes into the kitchen, drawn to the hum
of the microwave, before hearing movement

00:48:06.490 --> 00:48:07.570
from a closet.

00:48:07.570 --> 00:48:11.860
Before opening it, the contents of the microwave
pops, but meal that Michael is served is not

00:48:11.860 --> 00:48:13.210
the one he was hoping for.

00:48:13.210 --> 00:48:16.540
Because Laurie uses the distraction to bust
out of the closet and knock the knife loose

00:48:16.540 --> 00:48:18.570
from his hands using a fire extinguisher.

00:48:18.570 --> 00:48:22.910
How ironic that 11 fully equipped firemen
couldn’t manage to disarm Michael, but little

00:48:22.910 --> 00:48:25.220
old Laurie Strode with a fire extinguisher
could.

00:48:25.220 --> 00:48:28.930
However, he’s still able to grab hold of
her and smash her face against a china cabinet.

00:48:28.930 --> 00:48:31.990
He throws her down and stomps his boot onto
her throat, so she won’t be able to get

00:48:31.990 --> 00:48:35.300
out of this one by simply removing his mask,
because she can’t reach.

00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:37.390
Instead, she retaliates by kicking his other
knee.

00:48:37.390 --> 00:48:41.120
The tussle continues on, with one notable
moment being when Michael turns on the garbage

00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:43.570
disposal and tries to force her hand into
it.

00:48:43.570 --> 00:48:47.060
Not only is this an homage to a scene from
Halloween H20, but from Michael’s point

00:48:47.060 --> 00:48:50.590
of view, it’s revenge for their battle four
years earlier, where Laurie blasted off his

00:48:50.590 --> 00:48:52.110
fingers with the shotgun.

00:48:52.110 --> 00:48:55.770
This was probably the most damage that anyone
had ever done to him, because as I mentioned,

00:48:55.770 --> 00:48:58.770
Michael can’t just grow back fingers in
this timeline, so he’s looking to get even

00:48:58.770 --> 00:49:00.550
with her by mangling a few of hers.

00:49:00.550 --> 00:49:04.210
However, she’s able to get out of this with
a well-placed headbutt, and there just happens

00:49:04.210 --> 00:49:07.380
to be a knitting needle lying around, so she
tries that attack again, seeing as how it

00:49:07.380 --> 00:49:10.540
worked in 1978, but this time, he is prepared.

00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:13.570
Once again, he tries to get his revenge on
her, by impaling her face with the needle

00:49:13.570 --> 00:49:15.290
in the same spot that she once got him, and
this time he is successful.

00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:19.210
But, it comes at a cost, because this time,
she does manage to get close enough to remove

00:49:19.210 --> 00:49:22.800
his mask and the momentary distraction allows
her to pin his hand to the counter with his

00:49:22.800 --> 00:49:25.890
own knife, leaving him only one arm to work
with.

00:49:25.890 --> 00:49:29.850
She somehow manages to pin him down to the
kitchen island, reach into her own knife drawer

00:49:29.850 --> 00:49:32.140
and drive the blade into his heart.

00:49:32.140 --> 00:49:35.740
Ironically, this leaves him in a very similar
position to the one he left Phil Larson in

00:49:35.740 --> 00:49:37.160
four Halloweens prior.

00:49:37.160 --> 00:49:41.340
I discussed the possibility that Michael can
hold off the recharge period sometimes, and

00:49:41.340 --> 00:49:44.410
continue to power through to get himself out
of a critical situation, and I’m guessing

00:49:44.410 --> 00:49:47.920
that’s what happens here, because it only
takes four seconds for him to sit up, with

00:49:47.920 --> 00:49:50.460
so much force that he throws Laurie off of
him.

00:49:50.460 --> 00:49:53.660
With it abundantly clear that she won’t
be able to kill Michael, or even slow him

00:49:53.660 --> 00:49:57.390
down with recharge periods, her only option
is to try to immobilize him, which she does

00:49:57.390 --> 00:50:00.840
by pinning his other hand down to the counter
with the knife, and using the frying pan like

00:50:00.840 --> 00:50:04.780
a hammer to push the metaphorical nail in
metaphorical crucifix.

00:50:04.780 --> 00:50:09.720
He squirms when he realizes he’s now totally
defenseless, but just to be safe, Laurie also

00:50:09.720 --> 00:50:12.820
topples her refrigerator, pinning his leg
to the island.

00:50:12.820 --> 00:50:15.320
Michael is truly immobilized for the first
time.

00:50:15.320 --> 00:50:18.900
Even the trap she left him to die in at her
old home still gave him the freedom to move

00:50:18.900 --> 00:50:20.770
around the basement and eventually escape.

00:50:20.770 --> 00:50:25.700
Now, he truly could not go anywhere, and Laurie
takes advantage of the situation by grabbing

00:50:25.700 --> 00:50:30.410
her chef’s knife, the tool that Michael
favored and used to destroy so many families,

00:50:30.410 --> 00:50:33.730
and forced him to look at his own reflection
one last time.

00:50:33.730 --> 00:50:37.790
After all, if Deputy Hawkins’s interpretation
is to be believed Michael was never looking

00:50:37.790 --> 00:50:41.660
out the window at the Myers House, he was
looking in at his reflection.

00:50:41.660 --> 00:50:45.570
Laurie jabs her rival in the side, then, for
one last time, removes his mask, and looks

00:50:45.570 --> 00:50:46.610
into his real face.

00:50:46.610 --> 00:50:51.980
There is a supposed phenomena among initial
viewers of the original 1978 Halloween film.

00:50:51.980 --> 00:50:55.900
Many audience members reported seeing a deformed
face during the scene where Laurie first removed

00:50:55.900 --> 00:51:00.070
his mask, but in reality, it was just the
actual face of actor Tony Moran, with some

00:51:00.070 --> 00:51:03.860
spooky lighting and a small injury prosthetic,
meant to represent the damage that Laurie

00:51:03.860 --> 00:51:05.570
had done with the coathanger in the prior
scene.

00:51:05.570 --> 00:51:09.920
I can only imagine the blow to Tony’s confidence
was more damaging than anything any boogeyman

00:51:09.920 --> 00:51:13.810
can do, but the consensus is that because
of the atmosphere, the audience was projecting

00:51:13.810 --> 00:51:17.640
their expectations of horror and their own
fears when they watched that scene.

00:51:17.640 --> 00:51:21.940
The 2022 unmasking has the opposite effect,
because Michael really is kind of deformed

00:51:21.940 --> 00:51:25.880
at this point, through multiple stabs and
gunshots to the face, and of course, the blaze

00:51:25.880 --> 00:51:29.430
that seems to have melted his ear off and
left him with burns that nearly rival one

00:51:29.430 --> 00:51:30.880
Mr. Frederick Krueger.

00:51:30.880 --> 00:51:34.430
However this time we don’t get a direct
look at his face, leaving part of the horror

00:51:34.430 --> 00:51:36.390
up the imagination of the viewer.

00:51:36.390 --> 00:51:41.470
Laurie slashes cleanly through Michael’s
throat with a sense of finality… but Michael

00:51:41.470 --> 00:51:45.440
Myers is truly even closer to invincibility
than even she believes.

00:51:45.440 --> 00:51:49.900
He has to rip his hand out of the knife, effectively
splitting it in two, but it doesn’t matter,

00:51:49.900 --> 00:51:53.210
because he’s still able to grip his fingers
around Laurie’s throat, a vice that she

00:51:53.210 --> 00:51:54.690
cannot escape from.

00:51:54.690 --> 00:51:58.200
Strangely, she seems to egg him on from this
position.

00:51:58.200 --> 00:52:00.220
– Do it.

00:52:01.130 --> 00:52:02.240
Do it!

00:52:02.240 --> 00:52:05.790
– Four years ago, her granddaughter had a similar
line when Michael had her cornered at the

00:52:05.790 --> 00:52:08.610
Myers house with death as the only visible
outcome.

00:52:08.610 --> 00:52:12.140
But it turned out she was talking to her mother,
who was standing behind him with the pitchfork.

00:52:12.140 --> 00:52:16.280
Laurie’s words here are also directed at
someone else; this time it’s Allyson who

00:52:16.280 --> 00:52:17.660
gets to play the savior.

00:52:17.660 --> 00:52:21.550
She pulls Michael’s arm away from her Grandmother
and ****ing breaks it on the side of the counter!

00:52:21.550 --> 00:52:23.510
Wow I did not think she had that in her.

00:52:23.510 --> 00:52:27.681
With her airways free, Laurie slits Michael’s
wrist, which she seems to naively think this

00:52:27.681 --> 00:52:31.250
is the end of him when Deputy Hawkins arrives
on the scene with police.

00:52:31.250 --> 00:52:32.250
– Michael.

00:52:32.542 --> 00:52:33.582
– He’s dead.

00:52:34.427 --> 00:52:35.590
– Not dead enough.

00:52:35.590 --> 00:52:37.650
I’m glad someone has some common sense here.

00:52:37.650 --> 00:52:40.770
It seems like Allyson’s the only one who
is aware of the recharge period.

00:52:40.770 --> 00:52:43.460
Michael is moved to the roof of vehicle and
tied down with rope.

00:52:43.460 --> 00:52:47.295
I would honestly go with something a little
bit sturdier, knowing Michael, but that’s just me. 

00:52:47.295 --> 00:52:51.180
Police lead a procession towards the junkyard,
and many other Haddonfield residents join

00:52:51.180 --> 00:52:54.710
in to ensure that there’s no wiggle room
for Michael to pull some kind of miraculous

00:52:54.710 --> 00:52:56.850
escape, as he had in 2018.

00:52:56.850 --> 00:53:00.778
He is untied and involuntarily crowd surfed
to the industrial shredder.

00:53:00.778 --> 00:53:02.550
Carefully, he’s a villain.

00:53:02.550 --> 00:53:07.260
In the end, it is Laurie, the woman who lost
her best friends, her daughter, her son-in-law,

00:53:07.260 --> 00:53:10.981
and so many who were close to her, who rolls
Michael’s body into the gears, where it

00:53:10.981 --> 00:53:13.520
is completely crushed and shredded into bits.

00:53:13.520 --> 00:53:15.320
There would be no tombstone.

00:53:15.320 --> 00:53:16.350
No memorial.

00:53:16.350 --> 00:53:18.050
Only the legend of the boogeyman.

00:53:18.602 --> 00:53:23.690
But even with his body completely destroyed,
is this the end of the boogeyman?

00:53:23.690 --> 00:53:24.910
Maybe.

00:53:24.910 --> 00:53:26.608
But maybe not.

00:53:26.608 --> 00:53:30.289
(impact)

00:53:31.399 --> 00:53:35.390
(haunting piano music)

00:53:35.390 --> 00:53:37.690
Is this truly the end of Michael Myers?

00:53:37.690 --> 00:53:40.360
Has the Halloween franchise finally run its
course?

00:53:40.360 --> 00:53:44.720
Sure, they could always start a new timeline
branch or do another reboot, but for the purposes

00:53:44.720 --> 00:53:48.340
of this video, let’s focus on the 40-Year
iteration of Michael Myers.

00:53:48.340 --> 00:53:50.930
It is certainly the end of Michael Myers,
the man.

00:53:50.930 --> 00:53:54.511
We’ve seen throughout this timeline that
his injuries are permanent, and he gets his

00:53:54.511 --> 00:53:57.400
entire body ripped to shreds, so there’s
no coming back from that.

00:53:57.400 --> 00:54:01.920
But in Halloween Ends, we saw Michael’s
evil infect other people in the town of Haddonfield.

00:54:01.920 --> 00:54:05.890
It started with random crimes on Halloween
night, but it really took hold on Corey Cunningham,

00:54:05.890 --> 00:54:10.350
who started to go down the same path as Michael,
eventually developing an inexplicable desire

00:54:10.350 --> 00:54:14.390
for the mask, and even coming back from a
mortal wound after a short recharge period.

00:54:14.390 --> 00:54:18.210
We don’t see what happens to him, he’s
left laying in Laurie’s foyer and we never

00:54:18.210 --> 00:54:20.100
find out if he comes back to life again.

00:54:20.100 --> 00:54:24.070
If you’re not familiar, Halloween franchise
producer Moustapha Akkad created a special

00:54:24.070 --> 00:54:26.290
clause in the contract for each Halloween
film.

00:54:26.290 --> 00:54:30.330
The filmmakers were legally not allowed to
kill Michael Myers, so that Akkad could continue

00:54:30.330 --> 00:54:32.870
making money off the IP forever, which he
did.

00:54:32.870 --> 00:54:47.150
Which is why Michael’s apparent death in
H20 was retconned in Resurrection, the filmmakers

00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:50.170
made a deal with him where they were allowed
to make it look like Michael had died, but

00:54:50.170 --> 00:54:53.680
they had to undo it at the start of the next
film, so they came up with this whole scenario,

00:54:53.680 --> 00:54:57.520
where Michael switched costumes with the EMT,
and that’s whose head got cut off.

00:54:57.520 --> 00:55:00.920
It’s really dumb, but it’s also another
reason that Michael being unmasked during

00:55:00.920 --> 00:55:04.660
his death in Halloween Ends is significant,
because Laurie can see that she’s actually

00:55:04.660 --> 00:55:05.660
killing the right guy.

00:55:05.660 --> 00:55:09.770
Moustapha Akkad died in 2005, but I’ve heard
that his son Malek Akkad includes the same

00:55:09.770 --> 00:55:11.200
clause in his contracts.

00:55:11.200 --> 00:55:15.010
I can’t help but wonder if the ambiguity
behind Corey Cunningham’s fate was another

00:55:15.010 --> 00:55:16.530
deal with the Akkad family.

00:55:16.530 --> 00:55:21.250
Malek allows Michael Myers to meet his end
at 64 years old, and in exchange, Corey becomes

00:55:21.250 --> 00:55:22.250
the new Michael.

00:55:22.250 --> 00:55:25.180
Corey is 21, just like Michael was during
the original movie.

00:55:25.180 --> 00:55:26.840
So they could potentially start again from
there.

00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:29.130
I’m not saying that’s what I think is
going to happen.

00:55:29.130 --> 00:55:32.760
It probably makes more sense to just start
another timeline branch or go back to the

00:55:32.760 --> 00:55:36.780
anthology franchise idea and do some other
stories that take place on Halloween night,

00:55:36.780 --> 00:55:38.230
like what they did with Halloween III.

00:55:38.230 --> 00:55:39.700
That’s personally what I want to see.

00:55:39.700 --> 00:55:42.990
But aside from the potential contractual reason
that it ended as it did, I think there’s

00:55:42.990 --> 00:55:44.870
an artistic reason as well.

00:55:44.870 --> 00:55:48.290
Perhaps this was the end that David Gordon
Green and Danny McBride wanted, because of

00:55:48.290 --> 00:55:49.930
the message it sends.

00:55:49.930 --> 00:55:53.570
Perhaps they wanted us to feel like the evil
that drove Michael Myers is alive and well

00:55:53.570 --> 00:55:56.380
in Corey Cunningham, or even in somebody else.

00:55:56.380 --> 00:56:00.250
The opening credits of Halloween Ends show
a constant cycle of jack o’lantern rebirths

00:56:00.250 --> 00:56:03.330
and there’s also this scene where Lindsey
does tarot cards with Allyson.

00:56:03.330 --> 00:56:07.740
– [Lindsey] That just means a major phase is ending
and a new one is about to begin.

00:56:07.740 --> 00:56:11.800
– The most overused phrase in this trilogy was
“evil dies tonight”, to the point that

00:56:11.800 --> 00:56:15.270
it kind of became a meme, but if there’s
anything that I took away from the end of

00:56:15.270 --> 00:56:19.250
this Michael’s story, it’s that you can
stop one evil person, but you can never totally

00:56:19.250 --> 00:56:20.250
defeat evil.

00:56:20.250 --> 00:56:22.210
There will always be evil in the world.

00:56:22.210 --> 00:56:26.130
There’s no point in turning your house into
a fortress and obsessively trying to stop

00:56:26.130 --> 00:56:29.990
it, because there will always be another evil
on the horizon.

00:56:29.990 --> 00:56:34.071
If you enjoyed this video, I’ve also analyzed
the original timeline of Michael Myers, so

00:56:34.071 --> 00:56:37.410
if you’re interested in how that character
differs from this one, check out that video

00:56:37.410 --> 00:56:38.410
on the left.

00:56:38.410 --> 00:56:42.490
And if you love scary movies, that is exactly
what I cover on this channel, so go ahead

00:56:42.490 --> 00:56:46.880
and subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors
every week, ring the deathbell and select

00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:51.068
all notifications so you don’t miss any
uploads and I will see you in the next one.

00:56:51.068 --> 00:56:53.712
Assuming we both survive.

